  </div></div>
  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="integrity" data-keys="moderation thresholds quarantine auto reject comments threads nominations review queue" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Moderation thresholds<small>Where content scores (0–1) flip to review or auto-reject. Applies to comments, threads &amp; nominations.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <input type="hidden" name="moderation_settings" value="1">
    <div class="ad-form">
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="f-mod_q">Quarantine at ≥</label><input type="number" name="mod_threshold_quarantine" id="f-mod_q" min="0.05" max="0.90" step="0.05" value="{{ values.mod_threshold_quarantine|default('0.30') }}"></div>
        <div><label for="f-mod_r">Auto-reject at ≥</label><input type="number" name="mod_threshold_reject" id="f-mod_r" min="0.10" max="0.99" step="0.05" value="{{ values.mod_threshold_reject|default('0.65') }}"></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">Lower = stricter. Below the quarantine line content publishes instantly; between the lines it waits in <a href="/admin/moderation" style="color:var(--ad-accent,#237b22)">the review queue</a>; above the reject line it is blocked outright. Values are clamped so moderation can never be switched off by accident.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="integrity" data-keys="nomination eligibility threshold minimum distinct locations approve nominee" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Nomination eligibility<small>Require nominations from multiple locations before a nominee can be approved.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <input type="hidden" name="nomination_settings" value="1">
    <div class="ad-form">
      <label class="checkbox" style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px"><input type="checkbox" name="nomination_eligibility_enabled" value="1" {% if values.nomination_eligibility_enabled == '1' %}checked{% endif %}> <span><strong>Enforce eligibility threshold</strong> — block approving a nominee until they have enough nominations from different locations.</span></label>
      <div><label for="f-nomination_min_locations">Minimum distinct locations</label><input type="number" name="nomination_min_locations" id="f-nomination_min_locations" min="1" step="1" value="{{ values.nomination_min_locations|default('5') }}"></div>
      <p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">"Different locations" = distinct nominator country + state. The eligibility count shows on every nomination; when enforced, approval is blocked below the threshold.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
  {# ── AI governance ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Spend and agreement were both unmeasurable before: nothing recorded token
     usage, and nothing recorded whether a reviewer agreed with a suggestion. #}
  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="ai" data-keys="ai activity spend tokens calls today reviewer agreement capability model failure governance" x-show="show($el)">
    <div class="ad-card__head">
      <div class="ad-card__title">AI activity<small>Today's spend per feature, and how often reviewers agreed (30 days)</small></div>
      <span class="ad-chip ad-chip--{{ ai_enabled_flag ? 'green' : 'red' }}">{{ ai_enabled_flag ? 'AI on' : 'AI off' }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ad-table-wrap">
      <table class="ad-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">On failure</th>
          <th scope="col">Calls today</th><th scope="col">Tokens today</th>
          <th scope="col">Failures</th><th scope="col">Reviewer agreement</th><th scope="col">State</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in ai_capabilities %}
            {% set spend = ai_spend|filter(s => s.capability == c.name)|first %}
            {% set agree = ai_agreement|filter(a => a.capability == c.name)|first %}
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{{ c.name }}</strong><div style="font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">{{ c.purpose }}</div></td>
              <td><code style="font-size:11px">{{ c.model }}</code></td>
              <td>
                {# Declared per feature, not assumed: silent degradation is right
                   for optional writing help and wrong for moderation. #}
                <span class="ad-chip ad-chip--{{ c.on_failure == 'announce' ? 'blue' : 'grey' }}">{{ c.on_failure }}</span>
              </td>
              <td>{{ spend ? spend.calls : 0 }} <span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">/ {{ c.calls|number_format }}</span></td>
              <td>{{ spend ? spend.tokens|number_format : 0 }} <span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">/ {{ c.tokens|number_format }}</span></td>
              <td>{% if spend and spend.failures > 0 %}<span class="ad-chip ad-chip--gold">{{ spend.failures }}</span>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
              <td>
                {% if agree and agree.rate is not null %}
                  {{ agree.rate }}% <span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">({{ agree.decisions }} decisions)</span>
                {% else %}<span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">no decisions yet</span>{% endif %}
              </td>
              <td>{% if c.enabled %}<span class="ad-chip ad-chip--green">on</span>{% else %}<span class="ad-chip ad-chip--red">off</span>{% endif %}</td>
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {# ── WHY THE FAILURES ABOVE HAPPENED ─────────────────────────────────────
       The column to the left counts them. That count was the end of the trail on a
       host with no shell: "3" in a gold chip, with the provider's own refusal sitting
       unread in `gates_ai_calls.error` since the log was built. A rejected key, a
       decommissioned model, an egress block and a summary that ran out of time all
       rendered as the same chip, and each of those is a different fix.

       Refusals are deliberately absent — a spent budget or a switched-off capability
       is not a fault and has no provider error behind it, and listing them would bury
       the four rows worth reading under forty that are not. See
       AiGateway::recentFailures(). #}
    {% if ai_failures is defined and ai_failures %}
    <div class="ad-table-wrap">
      <table class="ad-table">
        <caption style="text-align:left;padding:12px 0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
          The last {{ ai_failures|length }} failure{{ ai_failures|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} in 24 hours —
          what the provider actually said, and the one thing to change.
        </caption>
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Outcome</th>
          <th scope="col">Tried</th><th scope="col">What came back</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for f in ai_failures %}
          <tr>
            <td style="white-space:nowrap">{{ f.at|when_zoned('j M, H:i') }}
              {% if f.latency_ms > 0 %}<div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">{{ (f.latency_ms / 1000)|number_format(1) }}s</div>{% endif %}</td>
            <td><strong style="font-size:12.5px">{{ f.capability }}</strong></td>
            <td><span class="ad-chip ad-chip--gold">{{ f.outcome }}</span></td>
            <td><code style="font-size:11px">{{ f.provider|default('—') }}{% if f.model %} / {{ f.model }}{% endif %}</code></td>
            <td>
              {# The provider's own words FIRST, then the interpretation — never only the
                 interpretation. A guess that displaces the evidence is how somebody
                 rotates a working key while the real fault is an egress block. #}
              <code style="font-size:11px;word-break:break-word">{{ f.error|default('no detail recorded') }}</code>
              {% if f.cause %}<div style="margin-top:5px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">{{ f.cause }}</div>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="ad-card__body">
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
        Every AI call is recorded in <code>gates_ai_calls</code>; the prompt itself is not stored, only a hash.
        Switch everything off with <code>ai_enabled = 0</code>, or one feature with
        <code>ai_cap_disabled_&lt;feature&gt;</code> (dots become underscores).
      </p>
      <p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
        <strong>Reading a timeout:</strong> <code>TIMEOUT after Ns</code> means the provider
        connected and was answering — the job simply needed longer than the feature allows.
        Nothing is wrong with the key or the network; raise that capability's timeout, or ask
        it for a shorter answer. <code>HTTP 0</code> is the different fault: the request never
        left this server.
      </p>
      <p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
        <strong>Reading agreement:</strong> a LOW rate is the clear signal — the suggestion is not earning its
        cost and the feature should be switched off rather than tuned indefinitely. A rate near 100% is
        ambiguous: it may mean the suggestion is good, or that reviewers are deferring to it. Treat it as a
        prompt to look, not as a success metric.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="ai" data-keys="ai providers api key groq gemini anthropic openai moderation heuristics test ai elevenlabs 11 labs voice speech audio microphone read aloud transcribe questionnaire" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">AI providers<small>Free-tier moderation &amp; AI features. The platform runs on built-in heuristics until you add a key.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <input type="hidden" name="ai_settings" value="1">
    {# This paragraph used to read "the first configured provider is used, in order:
       Groq → Gemini → Anthropic → OpenAI", which was accurate and is no longer how
       it works. Each feature now PINS a model by what its output is used for, and
       the pin is honoured; the key order only decides what happens once every
       declared hop is exhausted. Leaving the old sentence would have an operator
       adding a Groq key expecting it to take over everything. #}
    {# This named OPENAI as the pinned primary, falling back Gemini → Anthropic → Groq. That
       is not what the code does and has not been for some time: AiCapability::PRIMARY pins
       GROQ for all three tiers, because its relevant models are free-tier and this
       deployment's OpenAI key is not on a paid plan — a pinned call there 401s and burns one
       of only three attempts before anything can answer. Getting this backwards on the
       screen is how "Groq is hardcoded" becomes the reading: the pin is a PREFERENCE, and
       AiService::resolveRoute() appends every other configured provider after the declared
       hops, so a deployment whose only key is Anthropic still gets every feature. #}
    <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">Keys are stored server-side and never shown again. Each AI feature is pinned to a model chosen for the job — <strong>Groq</strong> first, because its models are free-tier and reachable, with a smaller one for throwaway suggestions — then falls back through <strong>Gemini</strong>, then anything else you have a key for. The pin decides preference, not eligibility: a feature only goes dark when none of them work. {% if ai_status.active %}Configured now: <strong>{{ ai_status.active|capitalize }}</strong>{% if ai_status.model %} ({{ ai_status.model }}){% endif %}.{% else %}No provider configured — using built-in heuristics.{% endif %}</p>
    <div class="ad-form">
      {% set ai_providers = [
        {'name':'openai','label':'OpenAI API key','hint':'platform.openai.com — <strong>primary</strong>: every feature is pinned here first'},
