      <div style="margin-top:14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e5eae8)">
        <label style="font-weight:600">ElevenLabs — read the questionnaire aloud, and let a nominee answer by talking
          {% if voice_status.configured %}<span style="color:#16794d;font-weight:600">● configured</span>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">off — the questionnaire stays text-only</span>{% endif %}
        </label>
        <input type="password" name="voice_elevenlabs_key" aria-label="ElevenLabs API key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="{% if voice_status.configured %}•••••••••• (leave blank to keep){% else %}paste your ElevenLabs API key{% endif %}">
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;margin-top:3px">
          <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">A nominee who can talk for an hour about the work of their life should not lose the nomination to a phone keyboard. With a key set, each question can be <strong>read out</strong> and an answer can be <strong>spoken</strong> — the transcription goes into the answer box for them to correct and send themselves, never straight into the record.</small>
          {% if voice_status.configured %}<label style="font-size:11px;display:inline-flex;gap:4px;align-items:center"><input type="checkbox" name="ai_clear[voice]" value="1"> remove</label>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px">
          <div><label for="f-voice_id">Voice <small>pick one your nominees will recognise</small></label><input type="text" name="voice_elevenlabs_voice" id="f-voice_id" value="{{ values.voice_elevenlabs_voice|default('') }}" placeholder="{{ voice_defaults.voice }}"></div>
          <div><label for="f-voice_model">Voice model <small>optional</small></label><input type="text" name="voice_elevenlabs_model" id="f-voice_model" value="{{ values.voice_elevenlabs_model|default('') }}" placeholder="{{ voice_defaults.tts }}"></div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:8px"><label for="f-voice_stt">Transcription model <small>for spoken answers</small></label><input type="text" name="voice_elevenlabs_stt_model" id="f-voice_stt" value="{{ values.voice_elevenlabs_stt_model|default('') }}" placeholder="{{ voice_defaults.stt }}"></div>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">
          The default voice is a placeholder, not a recommendation — it is an American one. Copy a voice ID from your ElevenLabs library and paste it here; for a continental African panel the accent is not a cosmetic choice.
          Currently reading with <code>{{ voice_status.tts }}</code> and transcribing with <code>{{ voice_status.stt }}</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px">
        <div>
          <label for="f-gee_make_url">Make.com agent URL <small>optional — lets Gee use an external agent &amp; its tools</small></label>
          <input type="url" name="gee_make_agent_url" id="f-gee_make_url" value="{{ values.gee_make_agent_url|default('') }}" placeholder="https://hook.eu1.make.com/…">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="f-gee_make_key">Make.com bridge key {% if values.gee_make_agent_key|default('') != '' %}<span style="color:#16794d;font-weight:600">● configured</span>{% endif %}</label>
          <input type="password" name="gee_make_agent_key" id="f-gee_make_key" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="{% if values.gee_make_agent_key|default('') != '' %}•••••••••• (leave blank to keep){% else %}shared secret (16+ chars){% endif %}">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;margin-top:3px">
            <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">Same key authenticates Make's inbound calls to <code>/api/v1/agent/gee</code></small>
            {% if values.gee_make_agent_key|default('') != '' %}<label style="font-size:11px;display:inline-flex;gap:4px;align-items:center"><input type="checkbox" name="ai_clear[make_key]" value="1"> remove</label>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:12px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" formaction="/admin/settings/test-ai" formnovalidate>Test AI now</button>
        <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">Makes one live call and reports which provider answered — the quickest way to confirm keys + network. Save any new key first.</small>
      </div>

      {# ── AND THE SAME TEST, ONE PROVIDER AT A TIME ────────────────────────
         "Test AI now" stops at the first provider that answers, which is what the platform
         does and the wrong instrument for "is Gemini working?" — a healthy Groq at the top
         of the ladder means Gemini is never called and this page reports a green tick.

         So a fallback provider can be unfunded, blocked by this host's egress firewall, or
         pinned to a decommissioned model for months, and the only symptom is that failover
         quietly does nothing on the day the primary goes down. This button stands on every
         rung. It costs one real call per configured key, which is why it is separate. #}
      <div style="margin-top:14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e2e7e8)"
           id="ai-probe">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" name="probe" value="ai" formnovalidate>Test each provider separately</button>
          <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">One live call per configured key, reported one by one — the only way to see that a <em>fallback</em> is broken while the primary is fine.</small>
        </div>

        {% if ai_probe|default([]) %}
