                  {% if p.cause %}
                    <div style="margin-top:4px;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;color:#3c4649">{{ p.cause }}</div>
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
                <td style="text-align:right;font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">{{ p.configured ? p.ms ~ 'ms' : '—' }}</td>
              </tr>
            {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <small style="display:block;margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">Measured just now, and not kept — press the button again rather than trusting this after you change a key.</small>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div>

  {# ── IS THE GOOGLE SYNC ACTUALLY WORKING? ─────────────────────────────────
     The same shape as the AI probe above, and for the same reason. Every part of this
     integration can be set correctly and still do nothing, and from the .env file all
     five failures look identical: the deployment was never published, it was published
     as "only me", SECRET and GAS_SECRET are different strings, the Calendar advanced
     service was never added, or the script was edited and never re-deployed — Apps
     Script serves the last DEPLOYED version, not the last saved one.

     So this asks the script itself, and every row carries the fix rather than a verdict. #}
  <div class="ad-card" id="sync-probe"
       data-sec="ops"
       data-keys="google calendar meet apps script gas url secret exec deployment interviews sync sheets"
       x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head">
    <div class="ad-card__title">Google Calendar and Meet
      <small>the Apps Script this platform books interviews and syncs sheets through</small></div>
  </div><div class="ad-card__body">

    {# ── WHY THESE TWO FIELDS EXIST AT ALL ────────────────────────────────
       They were read from .env and nowhere else, and there is no SSH on production. So
       the only way to configure the calendar was to edit a file the operator cannot
       reach — and every screen that depends on it said, correctly and uselessly, "set
       GAS_SECRET in .env". `gates_settings` first, `.env` still honoured as the
       fallback, so a host that has them in the file keeps working untouched. #}
    <input type="hidden" name="google_settings" value="1">
    <div class="ad-form">
      <div>
        <label for="f-gas_url">Apps Script web-app address</label>
        <input type="url" name="gas_url" id="f-gas_url" value="{{ gas_url|default('') }}"
               placeholder="https://script.google.com/macros/s/…/exec"
               autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
        {# Echoed on purpose. A stale /exec URL from a previous deployment is the
           commonest way this integration half-works, and it is invisible if the field
           is blanked for tidiness. #}
        <small>Deploy → New deployment → Web app, <strong>Execute as: me</strong>,
          <strong>Who has access: anyone</strong>. Paste the whole /exec link.
          The sheet sync uses the same address.</small>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="f-gas_secret">Shared secret</label>
        <input type="password" name="gas_secret" id="f-gas_secret" autocomplete="new-password"
               placeholder="{% if gas_secret_set %}•••••••••• (leave blank to keep){% else %}not set — calendar actions are refused until it is{% endif %}">
        <small>The same string as <code>SECRET</code> at the top of the script. Without it
          the script refuses to create events or read transcripts, so that nobody holding
          the /exec URL can book meetings in your calendar. Changing the constant in the
          editor does nothing until you <strong>redeploy</strong>.
          {% if gas_secret_set %}<label style="display:inline-flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;margin-top:6px;font-weight:600">
            <input type="checkbox" name="google_clear[secret]" value="1"> Remove the stored secret
          </label>{% endif %}</small>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# `formaction` on the button, NOT a nested <form>. This was a nested form, and an
       HTML parser DISCARDS a <form> start tag inside an open one — so the button kept
       its markup, lost its action, and submitted to /admin/settings instead. Pressing
       "Check the sync" saved the page and returned no rows, which reads exactly like a
       broken integration. The AI probe above uses `formaction` for the same reason. #}
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--ad-line,#e2e7e8)">
      <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" name="probe" value="sync" formnovalidate>Check the sync</button>
      <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">Read-only. Nothing is written to your calendar and nobody is emailed. The page is saved first, so you can paste the address and the secret and press this straight away.</small>
    </div>

    {% if sync_probe|default([]) %}
      <table class="ad-table" style="margin-top:12px">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for r in sync_probe %}
          <tr>
            <td data-col="Check" style="font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap">{{ r.label }}</td>
            <td data-col="Result">
              {# Never colour alone — the word is the signal and the dot is decoration. #}
              {% if not r.tested %}
                <span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e);font-weight:600">● Not tested</span>
              {% elseif r.ok %}
                <span style="color:#16794d;font-weight:600">● Working</span>
              {% else %}
                <span style="color:#a32b1c;font-weight:600">● Not working</span>
              {% endif %}
              {% if r.detail %}
                <div style="margin-top:4px;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#3c4649">{{ r.detail }}</div>
              {% endif %}
              {# The fix, and only when there is one to give. A row that prints advice on a
                 passing check teaches the reader to stop reading the column. #}
              {% if r.fix %}
                <div style="margin-top:6px;padding:8px 10px;border-left:3px solid var(--ad-gold,#d49a0e);background:#fffaf0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#5a4a1f">{{ r.fix }}</div>
              {% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <small style="display:block;margin-top:8px;font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">Measured just now and not kept. Re-deploy the script, then press it again — the result above describes the deployment that was live a moment ago.</small>
    {% endif %}
  </div></div>

  {# ── REFERRAL TERMS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     What a member earns for bringing a ticket buyer, and how many they need before it
     is payable. Both were class constants until now, so changing either meant a deploy —
     and the operator has no SSH. HANDOFF.md §4 asked for exactly this.

     The two numbers are NOT equivalent and the copy below says so: the rate is stamped
     onto each credit when it is earned, so a change governs future referrals only; the
     threshold is evaluated live, so changing it moves money that is already owed. #}
  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="money" data-keys="referral referrals commission rate threshold earn link code payout affiliate" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Referrals<small>What a member earns for bringing a ticket buyer.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <input type="hidden" name="referral_settings" value="1">

    <label class="checkbox" style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:12px">
      <input type="checkbox" name="referrals_enabled" value="1"
             {% if values.referrals_enabled is not defined or values.referrals_enabled == '1' %}checked{% endif %}>
      <span>
        <strong>Referrals are live</strong><br>
        <small style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
          Members get a link from their account page and earn on tickets bought through it.
          Turning this off stops new commission and stops new links being issued — it does
          not delete balances already earned, and links already shared keep working for
          the buyer. Individual events can opt out on the event form.
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <div class="ad-form" style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap">
      <label style="flex:1 1 180px">
        Commission
        <input type="number" name="referral_rate_pct" min="0" max="50" step="0.5"
               value="{{ ((values.referral_rate_bps|default('1000'))|number_format(0,'.','')) / 100 }}">
        <small style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
          Percent of what a referred buyer pays. Applies to <strong>future</strong> referrals —
          every credit already earned keeps the rate it was earned at, so this cannot restate
          what somebody was told they had.
        </small>
      </label>

      <label style="flex:1 1 180px">
        Referrals before earning unlocks
        <input type="number" name="referral_threshold" min="1" max="1000" step="1"
               value="{{ values.referral_threshold|default('10') }}">
        <small style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
          <strong>This one moves money that is already owed.</strong> It is checked live against
          everybody's count, so lowering it makes locked balances payable and raising it locks
          balances that were payable. Crossing it is retroactive — the whole balance unlocks,
          including the referrals before it.
        </small>
      </label>
    </div>
  </div></div>

  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="ops" data-keys="automation cron webcron maintenance run now schedule token reconcile credit paid votes pending payments queue cpi snapshots reminders" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Automation &amp; cron<small>Keep the platform self-running — no SSH or server cron needed.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <input type="hidden" name="automation_settings" value="1">
    <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
      The platform needs a periodic “maintenance” run (advance award cycles, drain the queue, recompute the CPI, purge expired tokens, snapshots, reminders).
      Last run:
      {% if cron_last %}<strong>{{ cron_last.ran_at }}</strong> ({{ cron_last.status }}, {{ cron_last.runtime_ms }}ms){% else %}<strong style="color:#b4452f">never</strong>{% endif %}.
    </p>

    <label style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;font-size:13px;margin-bottom:6px">
      <input type="checkbox" name="webcron_auto" value="1" {% if values.webcron_auto|default('') in ['1','true','on','yes'] %}checked{% endif %} style="margin-top:3px">
      <span><strong>Run automatically from site traffic</strong> — recommended when you have no cron. Maintenance runs in the background after a page load, at most once every ~15 minutes, so the site keeps itself up to date whenever anyone visits. Costs visitors nothing (it runs after their page is delivered).</span>
    </label>

    <div style="margin:12px 0">
      <button class="ad-btn ad-btn--primary" type="submit" formaction="/admin/settings/run-cron" formnovalidate>Run maintenance now</button>
      <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e);margin-left:8px">Runs the full hub immediately, once.</small>
    </div>

    {# The one task behind "I paid and my votes did not appear". A bank transfer to
       Paystack's checkout account settles minutes after the buyer has left the site —
       far too late for the callback — so those orders are ALWAYS credited by this
       reconciliation rather than confirmed live. It asks the gateway what actually
       happened, and only the winning pending→paid UPDATE credits an order, so pressing
       it twice cannot double-credit anyone. #}
    <div style="margin:12px 0">
      <button class="ad-btn" type="submit" formaction="/admin/settings/reconcile-payments" formnovalidate>Credit paid votes now</button>
      <small style="font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e);margin-left:8px">
        Re-checks every pending payment with the gateway and credits the ones that really paid.
        Safe to press repeatedly — it can never double-credit. Use it when a supporter says their transfer did not add up.
      </small>
    </div>

    <details style="margin-top:8px">
      <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600">Prefer an external scheduler? (optional)</summary>
      <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f);margin:8px 0">
        Point a free webcron service (cron-job.org, EasyCron) or a cPanel “fetch a URL” job at this URL every ~15 minutes:
      </p>
      {% if values.cron_token|default('') %}
      <label class="sr-only" for="cronUrl">Cron URL to schedule</label>
      <input type="text" id="cronUrl" readonly data-ag-do="select-all" value="{{ app_url }}/__cron/run?token={{ values.cron_token }}"
             style="width:100%;font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;padding:8px;background:#f6f8f5">
      {% else %}
      <p style="font-size:12px;color:#b4452f">No cron token yet — save this section once to generate one.</p>
      {% endif %}
      <label style="font-size:11.5px;display:inline-flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;margin-top:8px">
        <input type="checkbox" name="cron_token_generate" value="1"> Regenerate the token on save (invalidates the old URL)
      </label>
    </details>
  </div></div>

  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="integrity" data-keys="voting integrity disposable emails throwaway blocked domains mx deliverability otp" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Voting integrity — disposable emails<small>Block throwaway inboxes used to stuff votes. A built-in list + your additions.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">The OTP + registration gates already reject known disposable-mail providers. Add any new ones here (comma- or line-separated domains) to block them immediately — no deploy needed.</p>
    <label for="f-disposable">Extra blocked domains</label>
    <textarea name="disposable_domains_extra" id="f-disposable" rows="3" placeholder="e.g. newtrashmail.com, another-temp.io" style="width:100%;font-family:'Space Mono',monospace;font-size:12.5px">{{ values.disposable_domains_extra|default('') }}</textarea>
    <label style="display:inline-flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:10px;font-size:13px">
      <input type="checkbox" name="disposable_require_mx" value="1" {% if values.disposable_require_mx|default('') in ['1','true','on','yes'] %}checked{% endif %}>
      Also reject domains with no mail server (MX/A) — an undeliverable address can't receive the OTP anyway.
    </label>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:11px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">The MX check fails open: a DNS hiccup never blocks a real voter. Leave off unless your host has reliable outbound DNS.</p>
  </div></div>

  <div class="ad-card" data-sec="mail" data-keys="messaging sms whatsapp twilio meta cloud api sender phone number id access token notifications texts" x-show="show($el)"><div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Messaging — SMS &amp; WhatsApp<small>Nomination &amp; notification texts. Off by default; nothing sends until a channel is enabled and configured.</small></div></div><div class="ad-card__body">
    <input type="hidden" name="messaging_settings" value="1">
    <p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">
      Secrets are stored server-side and never shown again.
      SMS: {% if sms_status.sms %}<strong style="color:#16794d">● active (Twilio)</strong>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">inactive</span>{% endif %} ·
      WhatsApp: {% if sms_status.whatsapp %}<strong style="color:#16794d">● active ({{ sms_status.wa_provider == 'meta' ? 'WhatsApp Business Cloud API' : 'Twilio WhatsApp' }})</strong>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--ad-text-mute,#61728e)">inactive</span>{% endif %}.
      When both channels are configured, recipients with a phone get the SMS first, then the WhatsApp message.
    </p>
    <div class="ad-form">
      <label class="checkbox" style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px;margin-bottom:6px"><input type="checkbox" name="sms_enabled" value="1" {% if values.sms_enabled == '1' %}checked{% endif %}> <span><strong>Enable SMS</strong> (Twilio)</span></label>
      <label class="checkbox" style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px"><input type="checkbox" name="wa_enabled" value="1" {% if values.wa_enabled == '1' %}checked{% endif %}> <span><strong>Enable WhatsApp</strong> (Meta Cloud API preferred, Twilio WhatsApp as alternative)</span></label>
      <div class="row">
        <div>
          <label for="f-sms_twilio_sid">Twilio Account SID {% if values.sms_twilio_sid|default('') != '' %}<span style="color:#16794d;font-weight:600">● configured</span>{% endif %}</label>
          <input type="password" name="sms_twilio_sid" id="f-sms_twilio_sid" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="{% if values.sms_twilio_sid|default('') != '' %}•••••••••• (leave blank to keep){% else %}AC…{% endif %}">
          {% if values.sms_twilio_sid|default('') != '' %}<label style="font-size:11px;display:inline-flex;gap:4px;align-items:center;margin-top:3px"><input type="checkbox" name="messaging_clear[sms_twilio_sid]" value="1"> remove</label>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="f-sms_twilio_token">Twilio Auth Token {% if values.sms_twilio_token|default('') != '' %}<span style="color:#16794d;font-weight:600">● configured</span>{% endif %}</label>
          <input type="password" name="sms_twilio_token" id="f-sms_twilio_token" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="{% if values.sms_twilio_token|default('') != '' %}•••••••••• (leave blank to keep){% else %}auth token{% endif %}">
          {% if values.sms_twilio_token|default('') != '' %}<label style="font-size:11px;display:inline-flex;gap:4px;align-items:center;margin-top:3px"><input type="checkbox" name="messaging_clear[sms_twilio_token]" value="1"> remove</label>{% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="f-sms_twilio_from">Twilio SMS sender <small>E.164</small></label><input type="text" name="sms_twilio_from" id="f-sms_twilio_from" value="{{ values.sms_twilio_from|default('') }}" placeholder="+15551234567"></div>
        <div><label for="f-sms_twilio_wa_from">Twilio WhatsApp sender <small>optional, E.164</small></label><input type="text" name="sms_twilio_wa_from" id="f-sms_twilio_wa_from" value="{{ values.sms_twilio_wa_from|default('') }}" placeholder="+14155238886"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div><label for="f-wa_phone_number_id">WhatsApp Business phone-number ID <small>Meta Cloud API</small></label><input type="text" name="wa_phone_number_id" id="f-wa_phone_number_id" value="{{ values.wa_phone_number_id|default('') }}" placeholder="e.g. 106540352242922"></div>
        <div>
          <label for="f-wa_access_token">WhatsApp access token {% if values.wa_access_token|default('') != '' %}<span style="color:#16794d;font-weight:600">● configured</span>{% endif %}</label>
          <input type="password" name="wa_access_token" id="f-wa_access_token" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="{% if values.wa_access_token|default('') != '' %}•••••••••• (leave blank to keep){% else %}EAAG… (permanent token){% endif %}">
          {% if values.wa_access_token|default('') != '' %}<label style="font-size:11px;display:inline-flex;gap:4px;align-items:center;margin-top:3px"><input type="checkbox" name="messaging_clear[wa_access_token]" value="1"> remove</label>{% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--ad-text-mute,#5a6d6f)">Delivery is best-effort with automatic retries; every send is audited (numbers stored hashed &amp; masked). Recipients are normalised to E.164, compatible with Twilio and the WhatsApp Business API.</p>
    </div>
  </div></div>
  {# A search that matches nothing must say so. Without this the page just goes
     blank below the bar, which reads as "the settings are gone". #}
  <div class="st-none" x-show="q.trim() && matches() === 0" x-cloak>
    Nothing matches <strong x-text="'“' + q.trim() + '”'"></strong>. Try a field name (<em>otp</em>, <em>twilio</em>, <em>discount</em>) or clear the box.
  </div>

  {# Kept as well as the sticky one. Saving from where you finished typing is the
     habit; the sticky button is the escape hatch, not a replacement. #}
  <div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-end"><button class="ad-btn ad-btn--primary" type="submit">Save settings</button></div>
</form>
</div>
{% endblock %}
